# Author: Tigany Zarrouk (tiganyzarrouk@gmail.com)
#
# A biased IR run on the polar dimers, which straddle rank boundaries on
# purpose. The target is synthetic: what is under test is the mechanics of
# the bias -- that every rank agrees on whether to apply it, that the adjoint
# completes its reverse communication, and that the force is actually felt --
# not whether these dimers look like anything measured.
units           metal
atom_style      full
boundary        p p p
read_data       data/dimers_split.data
pair_style      lj/cut 8.0
pair_coeff      * * 0.01 3.0
bond_style      harmonic
bond_coeff      1 25.0 1.13
special_bonds   lj 0.0 1.0 1.0

velocity        all create 300.0 8712 mom yes
fix             nve all nve
fix             t   all langevin 300.0 300.0 0.5 4871

compute mu all mad/property/dipole charges 0.5 -0.5
fix     ir all mad/ir 2 c_mu nu_max 2000 acf_ratio 0.2 smooth 1 gaussian &
        correlate rate qc none &
        target ${target} fit yes yes fit_range 200 1900 &
        gamma ${gamma} warmup 200 bias_every 50

thermo          1000
thermo_style    custom step temp pe f_ir[6] f_ir[10] f_ir[11]
run             1000
